# No Competitor Names in User-Facing Text

- Never mention a competing extension by name in anything a user or AMO reviewer sees: extension UI strings (popup/options HTML, tooltips, notifications), `LISTING.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`/release notes, or the addon description/metadata.
- This applies even when a feature was directly inspired by a competitor (e.g. "the same trick used by X", "like Y does it", "X parity"). Describe the behavior itself instead, with no attribution.
- `ROADMAP.md` is the one exception: it's an internal planning doc, never shipped or shown to users, so citing competitor names/issues there for research purposes is fine and expected.
- Before finishing any change to UI strings, `LISTING.md`, or `CHANGELOG.md`, grep for competitor names to make sure none slipped in from roadmap research notes.
